# Pinterest Downloader

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Python 3.10+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10%2B-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-1.1.0-brightgreen.svg)](https://github.com/MohammadAliMehri/pinterest-downloader)
[![GitHub](https://img.shields.io/badge/GitHub-MohammadAliMehri%2Fpinterest--downloader-181717?logo=github)](https://github.com/MohammadAliMehri/pinterest-downloader)

Free, open-source **high-quality Pinterest image & video downloader** — CLI + local web UI.

Paste a pin, board, search, `pin.it`, or CDN URL (`i.pinimg.com` / `v1.pinimg.com`) and download the best available media:

- **Images** — `originals` → `1200x` → `736x` (auto fallback)
- **Videos** — progressive MP4 (prefer 720p) plus poster still when available

- No paid API key  
- No login required for public content  
- MIT licensed  

**Repo:** [github.com/MohammadAliMehri/pinterest-downloader](https://github.com/MohammadAliMehri/pinterest-downloader)

> **Not affiliated with Pinterest.** Automated access may conflict with Pinterest’s Terms of Service. Use only for content you have the right to download, at your own risk.

---

## Features

- **HQ images** — prefers `i.pinimg.com/originals/…`, auto-falls back if missing  
- **Videos** — saves progressive MP4 from `v1.pinimg.com` (plus `_poster` image) when the pin has video  
- **Pin / board / search / pin.it / direct CDN** URLs (images and direct `.mp4` links)  
- **CLI** with Rich progress bars (`pinterest-dl` / `pin-dl`)  
- **Local web UI** (FastAPI) — paste URL, preview grid with VIDEO badges, download  
- **Native save folder window** on download (Windows/macOS/Linux folder dialog)  
- **Concurrent downloads**, skip-existing, JSON output, optional proxy  
- **Python 3.10+**, offline unit tests  

---

## Install

### From GitHub (recommended)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/MohammadAliMehri/pinterest-downloader.git
cd pinterest-downloader
python -m venv .venv

# Windows
.venv\Scripts\activate

# macOS / Linux
# source .venv/bin/activate

pip install -U pip
pip install -e .
```

### One-liner (pip from Git)

```bash
pip install "git+https://github.com/MohammadAliMehri/pinterest-downloader.git"
```

### Quick launchers

```bash
# Windows — opens web UI if no args
run.bat

# Unix
chmod +x run.sh && ./run.sh
```

---

## Usage

### CLI

```bash
# Single pin (image or video — highest quality)
pinterest-dl "https://www.pinterest.com/pin/99360735500167749/" -o downloads

# Video pin → saves .mp4 + poster image
pinterest-dl "https://www.pinterest.com/pin/YOUR_VIDEO_PIN_ID/" -o downloads

# Direct video CDN URL
pinterest-dl "https://v1.pinimg.com/videos/mc/720p/aa/bb/cc/sig.mp4" -o downloads

# Preview only (no files) — shows Type column (image/video)
pinterest-dl scrape "https://www.pinterest.com/kentbrew/adventures-at-pinterest/" -n 20

# Board / search (first HTML batch)
pinterest-dl download "https://www.pinterest.com/search/pins/?q=minimal%20desk" -n 30 -o downloads

# Local web UI → http://127.0.0.1:8787
pinterest-dl web --port 8787 -o downloads
```

On **Download HQ**, the web UI opens a native **folder window** so you can pick where images and videos are saved (Browse… anytime). CLI option:

```bash
pinterest-dl download "PIN_URL" --pick-folder
```

URL-only shortcut (defaults to `download`):

```bash
pinterest-dl "https://www.pinterest.com/pin/99360735500167749/" -o out
```

Alias: `pin-dl` (same CLI).

### CLI reference

```text
pinterest-dl download <url> [-o DIR] [-n LIMIT] [-q originals|1200x|736x|…] [-w WORKERS] [--pick-folder]
pinterest-dl scrape   <url> [--json] [-n LIMIT]
pinterest-dl web      [--host 127.0.0.1] [--port 8787] [-o DIR]
```

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-o` / `--output` | Output directory (default: `downloads`) |
| `-n` / `--limit` | Max items (images/videos) |
| `-q` / `--quality` | Preferred image CDN size (`originals` recommended; videos always prefer 720p MP4) |
| `-w` / `--workers` | Parallel downloads (default: `6`) |
| `--pick-folder` | Open a native folder window for the save path |
| `--proxy` | HTTP(S) proxy URL |
| `--no-skip` | Re-download even if file exists |
| `--json` | Machine-readable output |

### Output files

| Media | Typical filename |
|-------|------------------|
| Image pin | `{pinId}_{title}.jpg` (or `.png` / `.webp`) |
| Video pin | `{pinId}_{title}.mp4` **and** `{pinId}_{title}_poster.jpg` |
| Direct MP4 URL | `{sig}_video.mp4` |

### Python API

```python
from pinterest_dl.service import PinterestService

svc = PinterestService(output_dir="downloads", preferred_quality="originals")

# Metadata only
scraped = svc.scrape("https://www.pinterest.com/pin/99360735500167749/")
for item in scraped.items:
    print(item.quality, item.image_url, item.video_url, item.is_video)

# Scrape + download (images and/or videos)
scraped, results = svc.download(
    "https://www.pinterest.com/kentbrew/adventures-at-pinterest/",
    limit=25,
)
for r in results:
    if r.ok:
        print(r.path, r.paths)  # primary path + all written files
```

### Web UI

```bash
pinterest-dl web --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8787 -o downloads
```

Open [http://127.0.0.1:8787](http://127.0.0.1:8787) — paste a URL, **Preview** (video pins show a VIDEO badge), then **Download HQ**.

---

## How it works

Pinterest does not offer a free public media API for this use case. This tool:

1. Fetches the public HTML page with a browser-like client (`httpx`)
2. Parses embedded GraphQL SSR / relay payloads, Open Graph tags, `i.pinimg.com` image URLs, and `v*.pinimg.com` video URLs
3. **Images:** rewrites to the highest quality path (`/originals/`, then fallbacks)  
   **Videos:** picks the best progressive MP4 from `videos.videoList` / `videos.videoUrls` (prefer 720p; skips HLS/m3u8)
4. Downloads from Pinterest’s CDN with concurrent workers (video pins get MP4 + poster)

**Board / search note:** public board and search pages only embed the first loaded batch in HTML. Full video URLs often appear only on single-pin closeup pages; grids may expose poster images only. Huge boards may need multiple section URLs or repeated runs.

**Video note:** progressive MP4 is supported. HLS-only streams (`.m3u8`) are not downloaded (would need ffmpeg). HEVC/trial ladder variants are deprioritized in favor of standard 720p MP4.

